{"data":{"body":"**[P2] Account for `XAmznTraceId` in checkpoint batch sizing.** This increases every instrumented invoke update's wire size, but `CheckpointManager.estimateSize` still counts only ID/type/action/payload plus 100 bytes. Near the 750 KB limit, the batcher can therefore submit an oversized request and fail the whole START checkpoint. Include the header's encoded size\u2014ideally all `ChainedInvokeOptions` and JSON overhead\u2014in the estimate, with a boundary batching test.","comment_node_id":"PRRC_kwDOQwbyFc751POl","finding_digest":"0a2b674e56024a02e8747fa62085f5e6093999eb274f804783875759e31e66a2","finding_id":"arf_v1_bivwotswajfaf2dup6tcbbpv4y","finding_key":"sdk/operation/invokeoperation::startinvocation::checkpoint-batch-size-accounting","identity_key":"sdk/operation/invokeoperation::startinvocation::checkpoint-batch-size-accounting","line":80,"observation_digest":"6e6fc4fa49f27db1de63bb2af098ad3f9a2105a48860f41c1dff23bac94e69af","observation_id":"aro_v1_nzx4j6sj6j63dxtdxmvpbgfnh6","path":"sdk/src/main/java/software/amazon/lambda/durable/operation/InvokeOperation.java","prior_finding_id":"","published_at":"2026-10-06T04:18:07Z","review_id":"arr_v1_dhw6gvtduzmnalnnioodpdv4eh","reviewed_base_sha":"ac6a6f5ea50d6a9098b716905f01c609e4c201ae","reviewed_head_sha":"5ae091e894f682952e5c19a71de44fb5a80d2552","reviewer":"codex","start_line":80,"suggestion_id":""},"pull_request":{"number":768},"record_id":"art_v1_qji2n7prr32y34hcmeieaslsla","record_type":"finding_observed","recorded_at":"2026-10-06T04:18:07Z","repository":{"full_name":"aws/aws-durable-execution-sdk-java","id":1124528661},"schema_version":1}
